    devices. The default event handled policy has been changed from `SuppressStateUpdates`
    (now deprecated) to `SuppressActionEventNotifications`, which keeps device state
    synchronized while suppressing action callbacks for handled events. [ISXB-1097](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/ISXB-1097)\n-
    Fixed all `InputAction.WasXxxThisFrame()` and `WasXxxThisDynamicUpdate()` polling
    APIs to use per-action suppression tracking instead of a map-wide flag. Previously,
    when multiple events arrived in the same frame with mixed handled/unhandled states,
    the last event''s suppression state could incorrectly affect all actions in the
    map. [ISXB-1097](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/ISXB-1097)\n-
